.Dd September 12, 2026
.Dt INTEL_RAPL 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm intel_rapl
.Nd Intel package power limits and power measurement
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To load the driver at boot, add to
.Xr rc.conf 5 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
kld_list="intel_rapl"
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver exposes the Intel RAPL
.Pq Running Average Power Limit
package domain, allowing the processor's power envelope to be read and, where
the firmware permits, changed.
.Pp
.Xr cpufreq 4
and
.Xr powerd 8
control frequency.
.Nm
controls power, which on a thermally constrained machine is the more useful
lever: the processor manages its own frequency to stay inside the envelope
rather than being held below a ceiling regardless of available headroom.
.Pp
Only the package domain is implemented.
.Sh SYSCTL VARIABLES
.Bl -tag -width ".Va hw.intel_rapl.pl1_watts"
.It Va hw.intel_rapl.tdp_watts
Package thermal design power, in watts.
Read-only.
.It Va hw.intel_rapl.max_watts
Highest limit the hardware advertises.
Zero when the firmware leaves the field unpopulated.
Read-only.
.It Va hw.intel_rapl.locked
Non-zero when the firmware has sealed
.Dv MSR_PKG_POWER_LIMIT .
Attempts to change a limit then fail with
.Er EPERM .
Read-only.
.It Va hw.intel_rapl.pl1_watts
Sustained power limit, in watts.
This is the figure that governs steady-state temperature.
.It Va hw.intel_rapl.pl2_watts
Short-term burst limit, in watts.
.It Va hw.intel_rapl.power_mw
Average package power, in milliwatts, over the interval since the previous
read of this variable.
Read-only.
.El
.Sh IMPLEMENTATION NOTES
.Va power_mw
is derived from
.Dv MSR_PKG_ENERGY_STATUS ,
a free-running counter of consumed energy units, so it describes a rate rather
than an instant.
Two reads separated by a few seconds are needed for a meaningful figure; reads
closer together than 200 milliseconds return the previous result instead of
dividing by a near-zero interval.
.Pp
Writes are verified by reading the register back.
A locked register accepts a write and discards it silently, so reporting the
refusal is more useful than reporting a success that did not occur.
.Pp
Limits below 5 watts are refused, as is any limit above what the hardware
advertises.
The limit register is updated read-modify-write so that the time window,
enable, clamp and lock bits are preserved.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Read everything the driver reports:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sysctl hw.intel_rapl
.Ed
.Pp
Measure power under load, sampling twice so the second reading covers a
meaningful interval:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sysctl -n hw.intel_rapl.power_mw > /dev/null
sleep 5
sysctl -n hw.intel_rapl.power_mw
.Ed
.Pp
Cap sustained power at 10 W:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sysctl hw.intel_rapl.pl1_watts=10
.Ed
.Sh COMPATIBILITY
Developed and tested on a Dell XPS 13 9343
.Pq Core i7-5600U, Broadwell-U, 15 W package TDP
running
.Fx 15.1-RELEASE-p3 .
On that machine the firmware locks the limit register, so the write path has
been exercised only against a refusal.
.Pp
Intel processors from Sandy Bridge onwards.
Support is detected by probing
.Dv MSR_RAPL_POWER_UNIT
rather than by a model table.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cpufreq 4 ,
.Xr acpi_thermal 4 ,
.Xr powerd 8 ,
.Xr sysctl 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared as an out-of-tree module in 2026.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Rafal Rabczuk
.Sh BUGS
On hardware where the firmware locks the limit register the driver can measure
but not intervene.
There is no way around this from the operating system.
